BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cablear-pcm5100@domosonica.com
DTSTAMP:20260203T120000Z
DTSTART:20260206T113000Z
DTEND:20260206T130000Z
SUMMARY:🔌 CABLEAR: PCM5100 al WeAct
DESCRIPTION:Conexión física PCM5100\n\nConexiones:\n• WeAct PE5 (SAI1_SCK) → PCM5100 BCK (pin 1)\n• WeAct PE4 (SAI1_FS) → PCM5100 LRCK (pin 2)\n• WeAct PE6 (SAI1_SD) → PCM5100 DIN (pin 3)\n• WeAct GND → PCM5100 GND\n• WeAct 3.3V → PCM5100 VCC (3.3V)\n• PCM5100 OUTL/OUTR → PAM amplifier\n\nVerificar continuidad con multímetro
LOCATION:Home
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Hardware,Conexiones,PCM5100,Día 3
END:VEVENT

BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:generador-tono-1khz@domosonica.com
DTSTAMP:20260203T120000Z
DTSTART:20260206T130000Z
DTEND:20260206T140000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 Implementar generador de tono 1kHz
DESCRIPTION:Crear lookup table para sine wave\n\nCódigo:\n#define SINE_TABLE_SIZE 48\nconst int32_t sine_table[48] = { /* precalculados */ };\n\nvoid Audio_FillBuffer(uint32_t *buffer\, uint16_t size) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i += 2) {\n        int32_t sample = sine_table[phase % SINE_TABLE_SIZE];\n        buffer[i] = sample;      // Left\n        buffer[i+1] = sample;    // Right\n        phase++;\n    }\n}
LOCATION:Home
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CATEGORIES:Código,Audio,Generación,Día 3
END:VEVENT

